+# Practice Systems Knowledge Map
+
+## Scope
+
+- Included collection: Learning
+- Included status: active
+- Hub note: K-101 — Retrieval Before Review
+
+## Synthesis
+
+The active Learning notes form a loop rather than a set of isolated tips. Retrieval comes first: attempt an answer before reopening the source, then correct it immediately [K-101]. Those attempts can be spaced with expanding gaps [K-102], while interleaving asks the learner to choose among similar problem types instead of merely repeating one procedure [K-103]. Together, these practices shift review from recognition toward recall and discrimination.
+
+Failures feed the next cycle. The error log converts a miss into a new prompt and records both its cause and corrected rule [K-104], while a jargon-free explanation exposes the first unsupported step [K-105]. That weak point can be revisited without rereading everything. The 1–3–7–14-day cadence is a personal starting heuristic, not a universal rule; after a miss, the next gap becomes shorter [K-102]. The hub note [K-101] therefore connects scheduling to error capture: retrieve, inspect the miss, create a better prompt, and schedule another attempt.
